  "Question": "If the data increase by approximately the same amount each time, which should be tried first?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "An exponential function model",
    "B": "A logarithmic function model",
    "C": "A linear function model",
    "D": "A constant function"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Assume that the input observations are equally spaced. A fixed increase indicates linear change: for \\(y=kx+b\\), equal increases in \\(x\\) give equal increases in \\(y\\). A fixed multiplier over equal input steps is when an exponential model should be considered first. Thus, under this spacing assumption, the approximately equal increases suggest trying a linear function model first, choice C.",
